    kind: work_item  # abd5
    title: "compact subcommand: --coverage flag is structurally dead-code in default connectivity-aware path (only effective with --no-connectivity)"  # abd5
    status: todo_hard  # abd5
    priority: 2  # abd5
    parent: INV-fanur-bumod-kopoj-gafar-nirat-bifig-mubov-fadik  # abd5
    tags:  # abd5
    - dogfooding  # abd5
    - compact  # abd5
    - cli_flag_wiring  # abd5
    - fold_audit_2026_06_03  # abd5
    isbefore: []  # abd5
    duplicate_of: []  # abd5
    not_duplicate_of: []  # abd5
    pr_ref:  # abd5
    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_2100_fold_audit_passes_21-40.md`, Family E). Consolidates F38.C1 + F39.B1 previously folded onto INV-fanur. Full evidence remains on INV-fanur's pass-38 and pass-39 discussion entries; this row provides discrete representation.\n\nThe audit's verdict: F38.C1's framing (\"silently ignored at cardinality\") was understated; pass-39 F39.B1 upgraded it to \"structurally dead-code in default path.\" The flag is not just ineffective at certain cardinalities — it's structurally unreachable in the default code path. Distinct fix-site from the other budget-coordination faces (INV-pazur / WI-fufop / INV-vopuh / WI-compact-selection-non-monotonic) because the bug is in flag-wiring, not in selection algorithm.\n\n## Symptom\n\n`compact --coverage <value>` is documented as \"Target centrality coverage 0.0-1.0 (default: 0.8)\" in `--help`. The flag is wired through to `CompactConfig.target_coverage` but is structurally unreachable in the DEFAULT connectivity-aware path. Code trace:\n\n| Path | Function called | target_coverage in signature? | Behavior |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `compact` default (`connectivity_aware=True`, compact.py:1046) | `select_by_connectivity(symbols, edges, seed_ids, max_additional, centrality)` at line 1050 | **NO** | `--coverage` value never read |\n| `compact --no-connectivity` | `select_by_coverage(symbols, edges, config, force_include_ids)` at line 1071 | YES (`at_coverage = coverage >= config.target_coverage` at line 905) | Coverage-aware as documented |\n\n**Pass-38 F38.C1 empirical (now superseded by F39.B1's code trace).** Tested cov=0.1/0.5/0.8/0.9/0.99 on /tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json with default `--max-symbols 100`. All 5 substrates produce IDENTICAL counts (100 nodes / 370 edges / 33 EPs / 16 features / 8 UCs) and BYTE-IDENTICAL file sizes (584496 bytes). SHA256 hashes differ slightly (internal ordering), but the symbol-selection cardinality is dominated by `--max-symbols` and `--coverage` contributes nothing.\n\n**Pass-39 F39.B2 noconn sweep (positive evidence of the corrected path).** With `--no-connectivity`:\n\n| cov | nodes | actual_coverage | Stopping condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0.1 | 57 | 0.1009 | coverage threshold (stops cleanly at 10.1%) |\n| 0.5 | 100 | 0.1966 | max-symbols cap (50% UNREACHABLE) |\n| 0.8 | 100 | 0.1966 | max-symbols cap |\n| 0.99 | 100 | 0.1966 | max-symbols cap |\n\nRoot substrate centrality is heavily distributed — top-100 nodes cover only 19.66% of total centrality. To make `--coverage ≥0.5` actually trigger in noconn mode, the user would need `--max-symbols >> 100`. No documented relationship between `--coverage` and `--max-symbols` in `--help`.\n\n## Invariant\n\nEither (a) `--coverage` is wired through to `select_by_connectivity` (e.g., as a stop-condition at frontier expansion), so default-mode users see the documented behavior, OR (b) the flag is gated on `--no-connectivity` in `--help` AND raises `error: --coverage requires --no-connectivity` when used standalone. The current state — silently accepted-and-inert in default path — is the bug.\n\nSame invariant-family as INV-rotup (CLI help text drift) but the wire-up is the structural fix; help-text update alone is insufficient.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nTwo paths:\n\n**(a) Wire `--coverage` through to `select_by_connectivity`** as a frontier-expansion stop condition (i.e., expand connectivity-frontier until coverage target reached OR max-symbols reached, whichever first). Restores the documented semantics for default users. More work but matches help-text claim.\n\n**(b) Gate `--coverage` on `--no-connectivity`** with an argparse `mutually_exclusive_group` or post-parse validation that emits `error: --coverage requires --no-connectivity`. Smaller patch; reduces user confusion at the cost of removing the implicit \"I can tune coverage\" expectation from default users.\n\nAudit recommends option (a) given the help-text reads as a default-path feature. The cousin row WI-compact-selection-non-monotonic (Family A) also targets the connectivity-aware path; both fixes could share a refactor.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F38.C1** — INV-fanur discussion entry 2026-06-02T22:16:17 (pass-38 batch; see paragraph beginning \"F38.C1: --coverage value is SILENTLY IGNORED at the cardinality level\").\n- **F39.B1 + F39.B2** — INV-fanur discussion entry 2026-06-02T22:51:36 (pass-39 batch; full code trace + noconn sweep; paragraph beginning \"F39.B1 (HEADLINE — UPGRADES pass-38 F38.C1 from 'silently ignored' to 'structurally dead-code')\").\n\nLab notebooks: passes 38, 39 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-fanur** (META: Sketch budget enforcement layered without coordinator) — sibling under same META to WI-compact-selection-non-monotonic (Family A), WI-compact-truncation-marker (Family A), WI-compact-summary-fields-disagree (Family A), WI-compact-induced-subgraph-incomplete (Family A), INV-pazur, WI-fufop, INV-vopuh.\n- Sibling: **INV-rotup** (CLI help text drift) — adjacent META; fix-path here is structural wire-up, but `--help` documentation is also affected and could be co-fixed.\n- Family E siblings: **WI-search-case-sensitivity-split**, **WI-verify-claims-silent-confirm-on-unknown-boundary**, **WI-verify-claims-inconclusive-on-typo**."  # abd5
    fields: {}  # abd5
